NMEA Cloud Framework — licensing

Safety information should not be confined to proprietary silos.
Everything in this repository is openly licensed so that anyone —
individuals, companies and governments — can read, implement and build on it
without asking permission or paying.

Different kinds of material use the license that suits them:

  Framework text
    All prose in this repository (the .qmd and .md files), except as below.
    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
    See LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

  Vocabularies and schemas
    Everything under vocab/, including term definitions and any
    machine-readable vocabulary, context or shape files.
    CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
    See LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt

  Code, tools, configuration and examples
    Build configuration, workflows, scripts, stylesheets, templates,
    and code or data examples wherever they appear.
    Apache License, Version 2.0
    See LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt

These licenses cover this repository only. They do not apply to data that
other people publish using the framework's vocabularies: the publisher of
that data chooses its terms.

Material from third parties (for example vocabularies the framework reuses)
remains under its own license, as noted where it is used.

Contributions are accepted under these same licenses, with a
Developer Certificate of Origin sign-off. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
